00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.760 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  both Diablo 3 and sacred 3 have been  streamlined since their last games to  make couch co-op multiplayer easy to get  into though Diablo 3 is clearly the  better action RPG sacred 3 does some  interesting things to make that couch  co-op experience as painless as possible  so which is the better game of the you  and your friends to flop down on some  cushions with and cut a swath for some  fantasy voids in Diablo 3 each player on  the one console can log in with their  own PSN or XBLA character if someone  doesn't own the game themselves they can  create a new character that is stored  locally and boosted to the level of the  other players  now this local character only has its  stats scaled it still actually starts at  level 1 it can hold its own in a fight  but it can't actually use any of the  loot that it finds until it's quickly  leveled up alongside the rest of the  party sacred 3 gets around this because  the game only rewards new loot at the  end of each quest that specific weapon  will always be rewarded at the same time  for each individual character so there's  no need for that loot to have a level  requirement now because of this when you  make a local character in sacred 3 that  character only ever exists for that  session if you come back later you'll  need to make a new character again at  whatever level the party leader is at  but you'll still have the same items and  skills available to choose from for  couch co-op this works far better  Diablo 3 supports for players in couch  co-op while sacred 3 only supports 2 in  order to reach sacred 3 is a maximum  play account of 4 you need to be playing  online however you can still use the  second players locally created character  in online play thereby allowing 2 people  per console or per PC to play in a  single online game in Diablo 3 each  player on one console can log in with  their own PSN or XBLA character even if  they don't own the game they just need  that free PSN or Xbox Live account if  someone doesn't have an account they can  create a new character that is stored  locally and boosted to the level of the  other players for Diablo 3 on current  gen consoles at least one player needs  to have an xbox live gold or PlayStation  Plus subscription to let locally created  characters play in online games on ps3  playstation plus is not required and  local characters can play online without  any issues on xbox360 every player needs  their own Xbox Live Gold subscription to  play online otherwise the game will be  forced into land mode which means you  can't play against other people  depending on your setup these  restrictions could be limiting if you  and a buddy want to play against two  other distant friends so if your couch  only has space for one other friend then  you've set with sacred 3 but if you're  King sized sofa needs warming then only  Diablo 3 will give you that 4 player 5  in Diablo 3 only one player is able to  view their full inventory screen at a  time the entire game stops and other  players have to wait their turn this  gets old really fast to compensate you  can use the d-pad to cycle through new  items without bringing up the full  inventory window but not enough  information is shown so it's hard to  tell exactly what each item does it's  inevitable that each player will  eventually have to stop everything and  sort through their full inventory at  regular intervals sacred 3 streamlining  makes its own inventory management far  less of a headache for other players  because new items and skill modifiers  are only unlocked at the end of each  quest never during combat the game  provides a set moment for you to manage  your inventory and at the only time that  you ever need to manage it both players  in couch co-op mode can see and sort  through their own inventories on the  screen at the same time as each other  with no need to stop and take turns  while sacred 3 makes headway in the  inventory management space Diablo 3 does  a far better job of managing each  player's physical location the game will  smartly teleport any player who wanders  too far to the edge of the screen back  towards the rest of the party because  all players need to be careful on screen  this means that someone can get up to go  and get a snack and the other players  can continue exploring because the  absent player will be teleported along  with the group sacred 3 includes no such  system so if one player stands idle at  the edge of the screen the other player  will be completely unable to move  forward until they return  though Diablo 3 is a superior action RPG  to seek for three it's not the perfect  couch co-op game having four players  take on the primeval on the same console  makes for a great time but it's time  beset by constant inventory management  interruptions and the need for all  players to have their own characters for  the smoothest result but if you're  planning on playing with a single friend  then say for three streamlining still  makes for a fun couch co-op experience  [Music]

